The source confirms that `AVCAST5` is an opaque, sole-owned context freed with `av_free`; initialization copies the key and retains no pointers. `AVCRCId` is a resource-free enum. I’ll keep CAST5’s private fields opaque and expose safe construction/reinitialization, plus a layout-compatible CRC identifier wrapper that preserves unknown values without publishing `AV_CRC_MAX`.
